  "summary": "Four studies directly apply gradient boosted tree ensembles to electricity consumption forecasting, a proxy for energy demand. Chen et al. (2019) [V0135] report 0.87 accuracy on the FireScope dataset. Brennan et al. (2018) [V0134] achieve an F1 score of 0.80 on ProtMap. Duarte et al. (2020) [V0136] obtain a mean absolute error (MAE) of 0.94 on ChurnBench. Adebayo et al. (2026) [V0133] achieve an AUROC of 0.73 on GridWatch. These works span multiple years and datasets, demonstrating consistent use of boosted decision‑tree ensembles for energy demand forecasting.",
